.TH ADMIRAL\-INSTALL 8 "July 2026" "Admiral" "Admiral Administration"
.SH NAME
admiral\-install \- Admiral platform installation and administration
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B admiral-install
bootstraps and converges Admiral nodes. This manual covers administration
workflows, security considerations, and common deployment scenarios.
.SH DEPLOYMENT TOPOLOGIES
.SS Single-node (evaluation or small production)
A single host runs all Admiral services: control plane, portal, worker,
database, and reverse proxy. Suitable for teams evaluating Admiral or
running a small number of customer instances.
.SS Multi-node with admin-portal and workers
The control plane and customer portal share one host
.RB ( \-\-admin-portal-node ).
Dedicated worker nodes
.RB ( \-\-worker-node )
run customer workloads via Podman rootless. Communication between nodes
uses WireGuard on 10.99.0.0/24.
.SS Split admin and portal
.B \-\-admin-node
installs only the control plane.
.B \-\-portal-node
installs the customer portal on a separate host. Each spoke requires its
own WireGuard peer and admiral-ssh identity.
.SH SECURITY MODEL
.SS Bootstrap SSH
During spoke installation the operator connects as root via SSH, creates a
temporary bootstrap user, and runs Ansible. After the Fleet\[en]Admirald
handshake is verified, the installer:
.P
  \[bu] Revokes the operator\[cq]s SSH key from the bootstrap user.
.P
  \[bu] Applies PermitRootLogin no via a drop-in configuration.
.P
  \[bu] Confirms that only the per-node admiral-ssh identity works.
.P
To preserve the bootstrap key for re-convergence, pass
.BR \-\-no-revoke-ssh-key .
.SS WireGuard isolation
Each spoke has a /32 route to the hub only. Lateral spoke\[en]spoke
communication is blocked. The WireGuard firewalld zone uses target DROP.
.SS Service hardening
All Admiral services run with systemd hardening:
.NoNewPrivileges ,
.PrivateTmp ,
.ProtectHome ,
and
.ProtectSystem .
Secrets are stored mode 0600 owned by root:admiral.
Admiral-fleet runs as root (required for Podman rootless management) but
drops capabilities via CapabilityBoundingSet.
.SH WORKFLOWS
.SS Fresh single-node deployment
.RS
.IP 1.
Install the admiral-common RPM and its dependencies:
.IP
.B dnf install admiral-common
.IP 2.
Run the installer:
.IP
.B admiral-install --single-node
.IP 3.
Wait for completion. The installer prints "Admiral installation completed"
and the Ansible PLAY RECAP with failed=0.
.IP 4.
Verify services:
.IP
.B systemctl status admirald caddy admiral-fleet admiral-flagship admiral-harbor
.RE
.SS Deploy admin-portal node
.RS
.IP
.B admiral-install --admin-portal-node --public-ip 203.0.113.10
.RE
.SS Add a worker node
.RS
.IP
From the admin node, SSH into the target worker host and run:
.IP
.B admiral-install --worker-node --public-ip 203.0.113.20
.B \ \ \ \ \ \ --ssh-key ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
.B \ \ \ \ \ \ --ssh-fingerprint SHA256:...
.IP
The installer connects as root, provisions the node, verifies the WireGuard
and Fleet handshakes, then revokes the bootstrap key.
.RE
.SS Add a worker node without revoking the bootstrap key
.RS
.IP
When reconverging a spoke that already has a healthy admiral-ssh identity:
.IP
.B admiral-install --worker-node --public-ip 203.0.113.20
.B \ \ \ \ \ \ --ssh-key ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
.B \ \ \ \ \ \ --no-revoke-ssh-key
.IP
The installer skips the revocation step and PermitRootLogin lockdown.
The operator key remains in the bootstrap user\[cq]s authorized_keys
for subsequent reconvergence runs.
.RE
.SS Deploy a portal node
.RS
.IP
.B admiral-install --portal-node --public-ip 203.0.113.30
.B \ \ \ \ \ \ --ssh-fingerprint SHA256:...
.RE
.SS Development evaluation node
.RS
.IP
.B admiral-install --dev-node --yes
.IP
WARNING: Exposes WSGI servers directly on ports 5000/5001. Not for
production.
.RE
.SH RECONVERGENCE
.B \-\-single-node
and
.B \-\-admin-node
are idempotent: running the installer again reconciles the node state.
.P
For spoke modes
.RB ( \-\-worker-node ,
.BR \-\-portal-node ),
reconvergence requires either:
.P
  \[bu] Passing
.B \-\-no-revoke-ssh-key
from the second run onward (recommended), or
.P
  \[bu] SSHing as the per-node admiral-ssh user with the delivery key stored
in /var/lib/admiral/ssh-delivery/<node-id>.ed25519 on the admin node.
.SH POST-INSTALLATION VERIFICATION
.SS Service health
.RS
.IP
.B admiralctl status
.IP
.B harborctl ping
.RE
.SSS Security checklist
The installer enforces a blocking security checklist on all secure modes:
.RS
.IP 1.
SELinux Enforcing with required boolean values.
.IP 2.
firewalld zones: public (ssh/http/https), admiral (DROP for WireGuard).
.IP 3.
nftables egress policy with default reject.
.IP 4.
auditd with Admiral-specific rules.
.IP 5.
fail2ban with sshd jail using nftables backend.
.IP 6.
chronyd with synchronized clock.
.IP 7.
Podman rootless with correct subuid/subgid, linger, user bus, and storage.
.RE
.SS Verify a running workload
On an admin or single-node host:
.RS
.IP
.B admiralctl instances list
.IP
.B admiralctl instances status <instance-id>
.RE
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.SS Installer fails with "Could not inspect the existing Admiral role"
The spoke has a previous installation whose operator SSH key was revoked.
Use
.B \-\-no-revoke-ssh-key
and the original
.B \-\-ssh-key
to reconverge.
.SS WireGuard handshake timeout
Check that UDP port 51820 is reachable on the hub public IP. Verify the
WireGuard private key on the spoke matches the peer public key on the hub.
.SS Fleet not registering with Admirald
On the worker node, check:
.RS
.IP
.B journalctl -u admiral-fleet
.IP
.B systemctl status admiral-fleet
.RE
Verify the fleet token in /etc/admiral/fleet.env matches the token in
/etc/admirald.ini on the admin node.
.SS Caddy admin API unreachable
Caddy listens on 127.0.0.1:2019. Confirm the service is active:
.RS
.IP
.B systemctl status caddy
.IP
.B curl -s http://127.0.0.1:2019/config/
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/admiral/role
Persisted node role identifier.
.TP
.I /var/lib/admiral/ssh-delivery/
Per-node SSH delivery keys, one per enrolled spoke.
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard/
WireGuard configuration including wg-admiral.conf and peers.d/.
.TP
.I /etc/admiral/secrets
Sensitive deployment secrets (mode 0600, root:admiral).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ADMIRAL_ADMIN_TOKEN
Authentication token for admiralctl.
.TP
.B ADMIRAL_INSECURE_SKIP_VERIFY
Skip TLS verification (Fedora dev mode only).
.SH NOTES
The installer requires:
.P
  \[bu] Enterprise Linux 10 (CentOS Stream 10, Rocky Linux 10, AlmaLinux 10).
.P
  \[bu] EPEL and CRB repositories enabled.
.P
  \[bu] KVM CPU support for rootless Podman (virtualization is acceptable).
.P
  \[bu] At least 2 GiB RAM and 20 GiB free disk for single-node.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR admiral-install (1),
.BR admiralctl (1),
.BR admiralctl-admin (8),
.BR harborctl (8)
.P
Multi-node setup guide:
